{
  "Document": [
    {
      "Heading": {
        "level": 1,
        "children": [
          {
            "Text": "OS API Overview"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Text": "Tauri provides a set of plugins and APIs that allow your application to behave like a first-class citizen on the user's operating system."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "Heading": {
        "level": 2,
        "children": [
          {
            "Text": "Beyond the Browser"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Text": "A standard web app is trapped in a sandbox. It cannot know the computer's name, cannot access files outside the browser's \"upload\" dialog, and cannot create system-level shortcuts. Tauri breaks these barriers."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "Heading": {
        "level": 2,
        "children": [
          {
            "Text": "The Plugin Architecture"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Text": "Tauri's functionality is modular. Instead of including everything in the core, features are split into plugins:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "UnorderedList": []
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "InlineCode": "tauri-plugin-fs"
        },
        {
          "Text": ": Filesystem access."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "UnorderedList": []
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "InlineCode": "tauri-plugin-shell"
        },
        {
          "Text": ": Opening URLs or executing external commands."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "UnorderedList": []
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "InlineCode": "tauri-plugin-http"
        },
        {
          "Text": ": Making native HTTP requests (bypassing CORS)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "UnorderedList": []
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "InlineCode": "tauri-plugin-dialog"
        },
        {
          "Text": ": Native save/open file dialogs."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "Heading": {
        "level": 2,
        "children": [
          {
            "Text": "Choosing Between Rust and JS APIs"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Text": "Most Tauri plugins provide both a Rust API (for the backend) and a JS API (for the frontend)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "UnorderedList": []
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Text": "Use the "
        },
        {
          "Bold": [
            {
              "Text": "Rust API"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "Text": " for secure, heavy-duty operations."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "UnorderedList": []
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Text": "Use the "
        },
        {
          "Bold": [
            {
              "Text": "JS API"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "Text": " for simple UI-driven tasks (like opening a folder picker)."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}